      "description": "Watch Watford vs Peterborough highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The Carabao Cup lights shone bright on August 25, 2026 , as Watford hosted Peterborough United in a fixture that promised plenty of action. Both teams entered the pitch with high hopes, aiming to navigate this tricky cup tie and progress further in the competition. A Nightmare Start for the Hornets The contest began in disastrous fashion for the home side. Just 10 minutes in, an unfortunate moment from James Clarridge resulted in an own goal, handing Peterborough United an early lead. Watford attempted to respond immediately through Mamadou Doumbia and Rocco Vata , but goalkeeper Alex Bass was alert to keep the visitors' clean sheet intact. Peterborough's clinical edge was on full display, and in the 23rd minute, Harry Leonard doubled the advantage with a precise right-footed strike from the center of the box. Despite Martín Payero 's best efforts to find a way back into the game before the break, the visitors remained resolute, heading into halftime with a commanding two-goal cushion. Second Half Blitz Any hopes of a Watford comeback were swiftly extinguished after the restart. In the 51st minute, Harry Leonard secured his brace following a clever through ball from Ben Woods . The visitors didn't stop there, as Bolu Shofowoke finished off a lightning-fast break just four minutes later to make it 4-0. The goals kept coming for the Posh, and in the 64th minute, Harrison Jones found the top corner from a difficult angle to extend the lead to five. Watford manager made several substitutions, bringing on Edoardo Bove and Othmane Maamma , in an attempt to stem the tide and salvage some pride. Consolation and Final Whistle The Hornets finally found a breakthrough in the 73rd minute when Mamadou Doumbia headed home from close range following a cross by Amin Nabizada . Doumbia nearly added a second late on, but his effort struck the crossbar. At the other end, Daniel Bachmann was forced into a late save to deny David Kamara as the game drew to a close. The final whistle confirmed a comprehensive 5-1 victory for Peterborough United , who march on to the next round of the Carabao Cup with a dominant performance that left the Vicarage Road crowd stunned."
